# Flow Performance Optimization Guide

## Flow-Specific Performance Requirements

### Speed Targets (Non-Negotiable)
- **Expense Entry**: ≤9 seconds (p95 ≤ 14s)
- **App Launch**: <3 seconds on budget devices
- **Screen Transitions**: <250ms
- **Data Sync**: Background only, never block UI
- **Offline Operations**: All core features work without internet

### Cultural Performance
- **Number Formatting**: <50ms for Bengali numerals (১,০০,০০০)
- **Language Switching**: <200ms for locale changes
- **Cultural Calculations**: <100ms for festival budget calculations

## Core Performance Principles

### 1. Const Constructors
Always use `const` constructors where possible to prevent unnecessary rebuilds:

```dart
// ✅ Good - const constructor
class MyWidget extends StatelessWidget {
  const MyWidget({super.key});
  
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return const Text('Hello');
  }
}

// ❌ Bad - non-const constructor
class MyWidget extends StatelessWidget {
  MyWidget({super.key});
  
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return Text('Hello'); // This will rebuild unnecessarily
  }
}
```

### 2. Optimized Widgets
Use performance-optimized widgets from [lib/shared/ui_components/performance/](mdc:lib/shared/ui_components/performance/):

```dart
// OptimizedWidget prevents unnecessary rebuilds
OptimizedWidget(
  child: ExpensiveWidget(),
  shouldRebuild: (oldWidget, newWidget) {
    return oldWidget.data != newWidget.data;
  },
)

// MemoizedWidget caches expensive computations
MemoizedWidget(
  builder: (context) => ExpensiveComputation(),
  dependencies: [data1, data2],
)
```

## Riverpod Performance

### 1. Use Selectors for Granular Rebuilds
```dart
// ❌ Bad - rebuilds entire widget when any state changes
Consumer(
  builder: (context, ref, child) {
    final state = ref.watch(featureProvider);
    return Text(state.title); // Rebuilds even when only description changes
  },
)

// ✅ Good - only rebuilds when title changes
Consumer(
  builder: (context, ref, child) {
    final title = ref.watch(
      featureProvider.select((state) => state.title),
    );
    return Text(title);
  },
)
```

### 2. Use autoDispose for Temporary Providers
```dart
// ✅ Good - automatically disposed when not used
final temporaryProvider = Provider.autoDispose((ref) {
  return TemporaryData();
});

// ❌ Bad - stays in memory even when not needed
final permanentProvider = Provider((ref) {
  return PermanentData();
});
```

### 3. Optimize Provider Dependencies
```dart
// ✅ Good - minimal dependencies
final optimizedProvider = Provider((ref) {
  final repository = ref.watch(repositoryProvider);
  return ExpensiveComputation(repository);
});

// ❌ Bad - unnecessary dependencies
final inefficientProvider = Provider((ref) {
  final repository = ref.watch(repositoryProvider);
  final theme = ref.watch(themeProvider); // Not needed
  final locale = ref.watch(localeProvider); // Not needed
  return ExpensiveComputation(repository);
});
```

## List Performance

### 1. Use OptimizedListView
```dart
// ✅ Good - performance optimized
OptimizedListView(
  itemCount: items.length,
  itemBuilder: (context, index) {
    return ItemWidget(item: items[index]);
  },
)

// ❌ Bad - standard ListView for large lists
ListView.builder(
  itemCount: items.length,
  itemBuilder: (context, index) {
    return ItemWidget(item: items[index]);
  },
)
```

### 2. Implement Proper itemExtent
```dart
// ✅ Good - fixed height for better performance
ListView.builder(
  itemExtent: 80, // Fixed height
  itemCount: items.length,
  itemBuilder: (context, index) => ItemWidget(items[index]),
)

// ❌ Bad - variable height causes layout calculations
ListView.builder(
  itemCount: items.length,
  itemBuilder: (context, index) => ItemWidget(items[index]), // Variable height
)
```

### 3. Use SliverList for Complex Scrolling
```dart
// ✅ Good - efficient scrolling with other slivers
CustomScrollView(
  slivers: [
    SliverAppBar(...),
    SliverList(
      delegate: SliverChildBuilderDelegate(
        (context, index) => ItemWidget(items[index]),
        childCount: items.length,
      ),
    ),
  ],
)
```

