## Animation Performance

### 1. Use Responsive Animations
```dart
// ✅ Good - scale-aware animations
AnimatedContainer(
  duration: context.layout.fast, // 90-140ms based on device
  child: child,
)

// ❌ Bad - fixed duration
AnimatedContainer(
  duration: Duration(milliseconds: 300), // Fixed duration
  child: child,
)
```

### 2. Optimize Animation Controllers
```dart
// ✅ Good - dispose controller properly
class _MyWidgetState extends State<MyWidget> 
    with SingleTickerProviderStateMixin {
  late AnimationController _controller;
  
  @override
  void initState() {
    super.initState();
    _controller = AnimationController(
      duration: Duration(milliseconds: 300),
      vsync: this,
    );
  }
  
  @override
  void dispose() {
    _controller.dispose(); // Important!
    super.dispose();
  }
}
```

## Memory Management

### 1. Dispose Resources Properly
```dart
class MyWidget extends StatefulWidget {
  @override
  _MyWidgetState createState() => _MyWidgetState();
}

class _MyWidgetState extends State<MyWidget> {
  late StreamSubscription _subscription;
  late TextEditingController _controller;
  
  @override
  void initState() {
    super.initState();
    _subscription = stream.listen((data) {});
    _controller = TextEditingController();
  }
  
  @override
  void dispose() {
    _subscription.cancel(); // Cancel stream subscription
    _controller.dispose(); // Dispose controller
    super.dispose();
  }
}
```

### 2. Use Weak References for Callbacks
```dart
// ✅ Good - weak reference prevents memory leaks
class MyNotifier extends StateNotifier<MyState> {
  void registerCallback(VoidCallback callback) {
    // Use WeakReference or similar pattern
    _callbacks.add(WeakReference(callback));
  }
}
```

## Database Performance

### 1. Use Efficient Queries
```dart
// ✅ Good - specific query
final transactions = await box.values
    .where((t) => t.categoryId == categoryId)
    .toList();

// ❌ Bad - load all then filter
final allTransactions = await box.values.toList();
final transactions = allTransactions
    .where((t) => t.categoryId == categoryId)
    .toList();
```

### 2. Implement Pagination
```dart
// ✅ Good - paginated loading
Future<List<Transaction>> getTransactions({
  int page = 0,
  int limit = 20,
}) async {
  final start = page * limit;
  final end = start + limit;
  return await box.values
      .skip(start)
      .take(limit)
      .toList();
}
```

## Network Performance

### 1. Implement Request Caching
```dart
// ✅ Good - cache network requests
class ApiService {
  final Map<String, CachedData> _cache = {};
  
  Future<Data> getData(String key) async {
    if (_cache.containsKey(key) && !_cache[key]!.isExpired) {
      return _cache[key]!.data;
    }
    
    final data = await _fetchFromNetwork(key);
    _cache[key] = CachedData(data, DateTime.now());
    return data;
  }
}
```

### 2. Use Connection Pooling
```dart
// ✅ Good - reuse HTTP client
class ApiClient {
  static final _client = http.Client();
  
  static Future<Response> get(String url) async {
    return await _client.get(Uri.parse(url));
  }
}
```

## Build Performance

### 1. Optimize Build Methods
```dart
// ✅ Good - extract expensive widgets
class MyWidget extends StatelessWidget {
